  "body": "`WebSocket.send()` sends the bytes in the buffer section referenced by an `ArrayBufferView`. Use that same section’s byte count for the `bufferedAmount` increment. For example, a four-byte view over a 64-byte backing buffer contributes four bytes. [Blink](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/a3dcf9eff1741c913166ea18149fe305f331e892/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/websockets/dom_websocket.cc#383), [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/main/Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp), and [Gecko](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/source/dom/websocket/WebSocket.cpp#2472) already use the view’s byte count.\n\nThe [existing offset-and-length test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/e3baabe076221e80d9c07d9aea2cbefa7ad656b6/websockets/Send-binary-arraybufferview-uint8-offset-length.any.js) exercises the view payload. An assertion for the immediate `bufferedAmount` increase could cover the accounting directly.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/websockets/79.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 1:00 PM UTC (8db0ade)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/websockets/79/7f25d7d...8db0ade.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 1:00 PM UTC (8db0ade)\">Diff</a>",
